// Test: bugfixes/sem001_static_method_arguments_class_declared_later
// Grammar: static_method_call
// Semantic: SEM001 — the arguments of `Class.method(...)` match the method's
//   parameters, wherever the class is declared.
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.174
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   error[SEM001]: A value of type string cannot be used as integer
//   sem001_static_method_arguments_class_declared_later.cln:15:
//
// Regression: the arguments were not checked when the class was declared
// after the caller (the resolver leaves the method unbound there).

start:
	integer f = Box.twice("x")
	printl(f.toString())

class Box
	functions:
		integer twice(integer v)
			return v * 2
